{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1072317-levels-and-cash","id":1072317,"title":"Levels and cash","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-02T19:40:56-07:00","id":1072317,"title":"Levels and cash","content":"So will pugmire be using xp or otger measures of advancement, and how will monies be handled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T01:48:05-07:00","id":1072408,"title":"","content":"Characters advance whenever it fits the adventure/story and the GM's judgment that characters should level up, so it's highly flexible and essentially tailored to suit each group, e.g. every adventure or so.<br /> <br /> Money is not really a thing at all; it's not an accounting exercise, it's about adventure and discovery. Characters are expected to have appropriate gear and to simply replenish stuff between adventures. They have a generic and vague amount of coin based on background, but money only matters when it's narratively important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12986-jargogle-bamboozle","name":"Jargogle Bamboozle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:42:40-07:00","id":1076080,"title":"","content":"I think, not mechanically but dramatically, it's treated like the resources background in OPP games. Like if someone comes from a certain background, they are expected to have a little more money to throw around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:07:15-07:00","id":1076922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1072317-levels-and-cash?p=1076080#post1076080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, not mechanically but dramatically, it's treated like the resources background in OPP games. Like if someone comes from a certain background, they are expected to have a little more money to throw around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's essentially correct. It's very different in the mechanics, but it comes from the same place -- money only matters if the player thinks it matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}